  clock: 4  # 09d5
  nonce: 09d5  # 09d5
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): Member candidate for INV-numat — exactly the umbrella's shape: \"similar names should encode similar concepts; when one construct is labeled two ways across emitters that's an axis problem.\" Sibling to WI-zadot (other half of WS taxonomy story — that item is about synthetic-node kind=function, this is about entrypoint kind=http_route). Code: entrypoints.py:152-179 EntrypointKind enum has HTTP_ROUTE + 20 framework-specific kinds (DJANGO_VIEW, EXPRESS_ROUTE, etc.) but NO WEBSOCKET_HANDLER; starlette.yaml:25-33 WebSocketRoute pattern emits to usage_contexts under a separate vocabulary. Two emitters (entrypoints subsystem and usage_contexts subsystem) operate on the same construct without shared normalization. Structural choice: (a) add WEBSOCKET_HANDLER + protocol-specific kinds to EntrypointKind for symmetry, OR (b) fold per-framework kinds back to HTTP_ROUTE + meta[\"framework\"]. Current state asymmetric and inviting drift."  # 09d5
